# Third-party notices

Sorta is MIT-licensed (see `LICENSE`). It links the crates below. Each is used
unmodified, as published on crates.io, and each keeps its own licence.

| Crate | Declared licence | Used for |
|---|---|---|
| anyhow | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | error context in application code |
| argh | **BSD-3-Clause** | command-line parsing |
| blake3 | CC0-1.0 OR Apache-2.0 OR Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception | content hashing, audit chain |
| chrono | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | timestamps, date parsing |
| flate2 | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | gzip compression for retention |
| infer | MIT | magic-byte file detection |
| notify | CC0-1.0 | filesystem watching |
| pdf-extract | MIT | PDF text extraction (feature `format-basic`) |
| serde | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | serialisation |
| serde_json | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | JSONL history, index, registry |
| tempfile | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | test fixtures only (dev-dependency) |
| thiserror | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | error taxonomy |
| tokio | MIT | runtime for the optional `index-turso` backend |
| toml | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | configuration |
| turso | MIT | optional SQL index (feature `index-turso`) |
| windows-sys | MIT OR Apache-2.0 | `GetDriveTypeW` on Windows |
| zip | MIT | OOXML extraction, `.sortapack` bundles |

Versions are pinned in `Cargo.toml`; the table was checked against crates.io on
20 Nov 2026.

